# 3. How do you prevent a python print() function to print a new line at the end.
# I can prevent the python print function to print a new line by adding the (end="") such that it ends by an empty string instead of the new line.
print("Hello World to the python",end = "") 
print(" this print funtion prints the line in the same line.")#this is the example of addition of a empty string at the end of a statement in print function 